### 1.3 Observations on v1.1

1. The four cross-cutting rows already operate as an OR over the type rows. A resuscitation on a member is notified under D01 and under DZZ. v1.1 never states how the two sets combine; in practice the union is applied. v2.0 states the union as the rule (Part 3).
2. Protracted is undefined. It appears on A01 (SDO) and A02 (five executive roles).
3. Location is named in the Procedure ("the location in which it has occurred") but has no column. The current paging configuration fans Area Response Officers out by area (ARO Western, ARO Port Phillip, and so on, with a Vic-wide fallback), so location is an operative dimension that the SOP does not state.
4. Type coverage gaps. No row exists for F01 to F03 (Duress and Rescue Equipment Activation), the T-series taskings (EMLO Deployment, External Event Attendance, Assist External Agency), Z97 Advisory Information, E09 Dangerous Surf, L01 Equipment Fault, 176 Medication Discrepancy, S07 Shark Attack Reported, E11 Generic Animal Incident, D21 Welfare, or Z94 Equipment Deployment. These are treated as NIL today by omission rather than by decision.
5. Internal inconsistencies to correct in v2.0: the Audience matrix names Area Lifesaving Ops Officer (LOO) where the Responsibilities and matrix use Area Response Officer; LSVComms and LSV Comms are both used; the State Agency Commander column header is split across lines in the published PDF; Related Information cites SOP 4.4 Activity Logs but the Activity Logs section relies on it without stating what must be logged for notifications.
6. Three type rows notify differently from their siblings for reasons that v0.9 moves into Tags: D13 Fracture and D14 Dislocation (SUP, ARO) against D16 Sprain or Strain (NIL); D09 Serious Bleeding (SUP, ARO, SDO) against D10 Laceration (SUP, ARO); D11 Needle Stick (SUP, ARO, SDO) against D08 Penetrating Trauma (SUP, ARO). All three pairs collapse to one v0.9 Type, so the notification difference survives only as a Tag rule.
7. Resuscitation is a type in v1.1 and a Tag in v0.9. Under the v0.9 precedence rule a rescue with a resuscitation is a Rescue (v1.1 reach three roles), so without a Tag rule the executive notifications for a resuscitation would be lost on every rescue.

