## Part 2. Trigger model

### 2.1 Definitions

A **trigger** is a fact about an incident that, when present, subscribes one or more roles to that incident. Triggers are of seven kinds. Every notification rule in v2.0 is a trigger paired with a set of roles.

| Kind | Source in the v0.9 model | Evaluated |
|---|---|---|
| Type | Incident Type node in the tree; a rule on a node applies to every descendant unless marked node-only | At open, at refinement, at correction |
| Tag | A controlled Tag on the incident | When the Tag is added |
| Outcome | Incident Outcome value | When the Outcome is set |
| Condition | A measurable state of the incident, currently Protracted | When the condition becomes true |
| Area | The incident's Area, or the Area of any attached unit | At open and whenever a unit is attached |
| Derived | A count or flag computed from LIMSOC fields | Whenever the underlying field changes |
| Manual | An action by the LSV Comms Supervisor | When taken |

### 2.2 Type triggers

Type rules attach to nodes of the v0.9 tree. Inheritance applies: a rule on Search And Rescue applies to every Search, Rescue and Emergency child. A child may add roles; a child never removes roles inherited from its parent. Where an incident is opened at a Not Final node, the rule on that node applies at open, and the rules of the child apply when the incident is refined. Refinement adds; it never removes.

### 2.3 Tag triggers

A Tag rule fires when the Tag is added, regardless of the Type. Tags used as triggers must exist in the controlled Tag taxonomy (Incident Labels, priority 1.8). Tags this SOP requires that are not yet in the v0.9 draft groups are listed in Part 2.9 as requests to 1.8.

### 2.4 Outcome triggers

An Outcome rule fires when the Outcome is set. The Outcome may be set as soon as it is known and is required at closure (N. Wood, 30 Aug 2026; the v0.9 pack wording "a required selection when closing an incident" is to be read as required at closure, not restricted to closure). Outcome values are gated by Type in v0.9; an Outcome rule therefore applies only to the Types that can produce that Outcome.

### 2.5 Condition trigger: Protracted

An incident is Protracted when 60 minutes have elapsed since the Agency Status was first set to Responding without the Agency Status reaching Under Control. The condition is evaluated by the platform and fires once. Protracted rules attach to Type nodes and apply to descendants in the same way as Type rules.

Decision (N. Wood, 30 Aug 2026): 60 minute threshold confirmed; to be stated explicitly in the SOP.

### 2.6 Area trigger

An Area Response Officer is subscribed to an incident when either condition holds: the incident is located in that officer's Area, or a unit from that officer's Area is attached to the incident. Both conditions are evaluated at open and re-evaluated whenever a unit is attached. Where the incident Area cannot be resolved, the Vic-wide fallback applies.

Decision (N. Wood, 30 Aug 2026): both conditions confirmed.

In the matrix (Part 4), an entry in the ARO column means the ARO or AROs resolved by this rule.

### 2.7 Derived and manual triggers

| Trigger | Definition | v1.1 origin |
|---|---|---|
| State resource tasked | One or more state-level assets (helicopter, RWC, ERU, drone, state vehicle) attached as a responding unit | ZZZ Any Incident Utilising State Resources |
| Multiple services responding | Two or more lifesaving services (clubs or lifeguard services) attached as responding units | ZZZ Any Incident Involving More Than One Club or Service |
| Supervisor add | The LSV Comms Supervisor subscribes any role or unit to any incident at any time, recorded in the incident chronology | B99 and Z99 discretion cells, "As Required" cells |

Media interest is a Tag (Part 2.9), raised manually, and is therefore a Tag trigger rather than a manual trigger.

### 2.8 Not Final and refinement

An incident opened at a Not Final node (for example Medical, or Search And Rescue > Search > Person) subscribes the roles on that node at open. Refinement to a child adds the child's roles. Correction of a miscategorised Type (v0.9 Rule 1) adds the roles of the corrected Type; roles subscribed under the incorrect Type remain subscribed unless cleared by the Supervisor (Part 3.4).

