## Part 5. Platform requirements arising (for the v0.9 pack Annex C and Feature Brief 012)

Feature Brief LIMSOC-BRIEF-LSV-2026-012 states that notifications must be configurable on type, tag, agency status and outcome. This SOP requires the following in addition.

1. Type rules inherit down the tree; a node may be marked node-only.
2. Rules on Tags, Outcomes, a Protracted timer (minutes since Responding without Under Control), Area of incident, Area of attached unit, state resource tasked, and count of responding services.
3. A per-incident subscription list, persisted with the incident, computed as the union of all rules that have fired, plus Supervisor additions.
4. Every notifiable event (Part 3.3) is sent to the whole subscription list; a newly added subscriber receives an incident summary first.
5. Clearing of any subscriber at any time by LSV Comms, with the clearing recorded in the chronology.
6. All notifications sent, and all subscription changes, are recorded in the incident chronology with time, method and operator.
7. Rules and recipients are configurable in the administrative portal without redevelopment.
8. Tags requested from Incident Labels (1.8): Media Interest, plus confirmation that Needle Stick, Spinal, Fracture, Dislocation and Attack Reported are in the taxonomy.
